'''Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarō: Yōkai Dotabata Daisensō''' (ゆる～いゲゲゲの鬼太郎 妖怪ドタバタ大戦争, "'''Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarō: The Great Yōkai Slapstick War'''"), also known as just '''YuruGeGe''' (ゆるゲゲ) or '''YuruKita''' (ゆるきた), was a Japanese-exclusive tower defense game released for the 50th anniversary (Nov. 1st, 2018) of the [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:GeGeGe no Kitarō (Series)|GeGeGe no Kitarō]] franchise. Developed by [[PONOS Corporation|PONOS]] and [[wikipedia:DeNA|DeNA]], YuruGeGe played very similarly to [[The Battle Cats]], but in many ways was more polished due to being a more recent game.

As of January 16th, 2023, the game has been discontinued and can no longer be downloaded.

==What is GeGeGe no Kitarō?==
The GeGeGe no Kitarō series chronicles the adventures of [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Kitarō|Kitarō]], who strives to maintain peace between humans and [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Yōkai|Yōkai]]. Beginning as ''[[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Hakaba Kitarō|Hakaba Kitarō]]'', a kamishibai written by World War II veteran, mangaka and ''[[wikipedia:Yōkai|yōkai]]'' enthusiast [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Shigeru Mizuki|Shigeru Mizuki]] in 1960, the series helped reignite interest in ''yōkai'' throughout Japan and spawned countless games, anime, movies, novels, merchandise, and even a [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:GeGeGe no Kitarō Wiki|wiki]] with over 3,000 articles.

For an in-depth look at the franchise's history, see these articles:

*[[wikipedia:GeGeGe no Kitarō|Wikipedia article]]
*[[wikia:gegegenokitaro:GeGeGe no Kitarō (Series)|Fandom article]]
*[[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Hakaba Kitarō|Hakaba Kitarō]]

==Gameplay==
Gameplay was best described as [[The Battle Cats]] cranked up to eleven—more polished but even more unforgiving. While the game itself played almost the same, unit stats were generally more ''extreme'' than in The Battle Cats, and there were many challenging new enemy types, abilities and mechanics to learn. However, the game was also filled with numerous "quality of life" improvements, including a more detailed Character Guide which showed units' exact stats and abilities, and a more in-depth "Enemies Appearing" window that also showed said info as well as strength magnifications.

==Characters==
As its name suggests, YuruGeGe used the character designs from the [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarō|Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarō]] line of merchandise and LINE stickers, hence most of them were based on their [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:GeGeGe no Kitarō (2007)|2007 anime]] depictions. Playable characters were listed in the Team Yuru-i (ゆる～い団 ''Yuru-i-dan'') section of the Character Guide, ''yurui'' meaning "loose", "lenient", or "easy" (as in "take it easy"), while enemies were found under Team Yaba-i (やば～い団 ''Yaba-i-dan''), ''yabai'' meaning "dangerous", "risky", "highly concerning", etc.

===Playable===
A wide range of friendly [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:GeGeGe no Kitarō Wiki|GeGeGe no Kitarō]] faces major, minor and everything in between appeared as allies, including the many iterations of [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Kitarō|Kitarō]], [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Medama-Oyaji|Medama-Oyaji]] and [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Neko-Musume|Neko-Musume]] as well as characters like [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Aoi|Aoi]], [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Aobōzu|Aobōzu]] and [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Nezumi-Otoko|Nezumi-Otoko]]. Allies were sorted into six rarities: [https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/t/%B4%F0%CB%DC Normal], [https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/t/%A5%EC%A5%A2 Rare], [https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/t/%B7%E3%A5%EC%A5%A2 Super Rare], [https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/t/%C4%B6%B7%E3%A5%EC%A5%A2 Uber Rare], [https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/t/%C5%C1%C0%E2%A5%EC%A5%A2 Legend Rare] and [https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/t/sp SP] (Special).

An outdated list of playable characters can be found [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:List of Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarō: Yōkai Dotabata Daisensō playable characters|here]].

====Roles====
Playable characters had an official [[Classification|classification]] system called '''roles''' (ロール ''rōru''). The filter allowed players to sort units by role in addition to rarity, targeted trait, abilities and type, making it easier to find units of specific classifications.

Some units had multiple roles or even changed role as they evolved. For example, [https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/d/%A4%CC%A4%EA%A4%AB%A4%D9 Nurikabe]'s Normal and Evolved Forms had both Attacker and Tank roles, while his [[True Form]], Nuristal, was purely a Tank, trading most of his attack power, health, cost-efficiency and recharge speed for the Metal ability.
