===Enemies===
The enemy lineup was a whole rogues gallery of antagonistic [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Yōkai|Yōkai]] from all parts of the GeGeGe no Kitarō franchise, including [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Backbeard|Backbeard]], [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Nurarihyon|Nurarihyon]], [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Shu-no-Bon|Shu-no-Bon]], [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Vampire Elite|Vampire Elite (Johnny)]], [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Zambia|Zambia]], [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Vodyanoy|Vodyanoy]] and many more. For the most part, enemy variants were grouped together in the Character Guide, even if some were introduced much later than others: the first enemy listed was [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Maruge|Maruge]], followed by each of his traited variants; next came [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Kemedama|Kemedama]] and his variants, etc. Those who had multiple traits at a time were always listed after those with only one.

Some bosses in this game had multiple phases. An example is [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Qi|Qi]], who would switch to his [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Kitsune|Nine-Tailed Fox]] form upon being defeated in certain stages.

An outdated list of enemies can be found [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:List of Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarō: Yōkai Dotabata Daisensō enemy characters|here]].

