==Stages==
*'''Story''' (物語 ''Monogatari''): Just like The Battle Cats, YuruGeGe had three main story arcs with three chapters each. Rather than having 48 stages in every chapter, YuruGeGe had 50-52 stages per chapter. Every chapter of each arc added one more stage: the chapter 1s had 50 stages, chapter 2s had 51 stages, and chapter 3s had 52 stages. [[Treasure]]s were dropped by a specific enemy in each stage.
**'''[https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/d/%c6%fc%cb%dc%ca%d4 Japan Arc]''' (日本編 ''Nihon-hen''): The only arc available at the beginning dealt with the hostile [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Yōkai|Yōkai]] rampaging throughout Japan, culminating in a fight against [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Nurarihyon|Nurarihyon]] and [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Kani-Bōzu|Kani-Bozu]] at the end of Chapter 3. Unlike [[Empire of Cats]], most of the stages had different enemies between chapters, not just the final stages.
**'''[https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/d/%c0%a4%b3%a6%ca%d4 World Arc]''' (世界編 ''Sekai-hen''): At its name implied, the World Arc took place all across the world, introducing the Serious enemies and most of the [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Western Yōkai|Western Yōkai]]; Chapter 3 of this arc introduced Forcefields, animated enemy bases, the Death trait and the first dual-trait enemies, ending with [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Backbeard|Backbeard]] as the final boss.
**'''[https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/d/%c3%cf%b9%f6%ca%d4 Jigoku Arc]''' (地獄編 ''Jigoku-hen''): This arc only had one chapter released before the game was shut down, which took place in [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Jigoku|Jigoku]] itself and featured many Death enemies as well as [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Akuma|Akuma]] like [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Belial|Belial]], pitting [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Kitarō|Kitarō]] and friends against [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Enma-Daiō|Enma-Daiō]] in the final stage. Like [[Cats of the Cosmos]], most stages in this arc had restrictions.
*'''[https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/d/%b3%b0%c5%c1 Gaiden]''' (外伝): Roughly meaning "Side Story" or "Another Story", Gaiden stages were the equivalent of [[Legend Stages|Stories of Legend]]. Taking place in another dimension with new enemies, a total of 35 sub-chapters were released for this mode. Each sub-chapter had 5-7 stages, some of which dropped exclusive Special units. They were available in 4 difficulty levels, applying different strength magnifications and rarity restrictions depending on the sub-chapter:
