*'''[https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/d/%a5%b2%a5%b2%a5%b2%bb%cb GeGeGe Histories]''' (ゲゲゲ史 ''GeGeGe-shi''): 11 extra-difficult mini-chapters based on story arcs from the 4th, 5th and 6th GeGeGe no Kitarō anime series, with 31 new enemies and high buffs on old ones. Chapter 1 had 1 stage, but the rest had 5-10 stages. Unlike Gaiden, GeGeGe Histories had its own Treasures, and some stages also had non-rarity-based restrictions which only allowed you to deploy units of certain types.
*'''Event''' (イベント ''Ibento''): Time-limited event stages with their own challenges and rewards, including monthly and seasonal events, [[:Category:Awakening Stages|Awakening Stages]], [[:Category:Advent Stages|Advent Stages]], [[Collaboration Events]] and more.
**'''[https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/d/%A5%CE%A5%A4%A5%BA%A1%A6%A5%CF%A5%B6%A1%BC%A5%C9 Noise Hazard]''' (ノイズ・ハザード ''Noizu Hazādo''): A trilogy of event chapters that introduced the Noise and Virus traits and had its own opening like the main stages. Each chapter had 4 difficulties, with ★3 restricting units by rarity and ★4 restricting units by type.
**'''[https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/d/%cb%bd%c1%f6%a5%a4%a5%d9%a5%f3%a5%c8 Rampage Event]''' (暴走イベント ''Bōsō Ibento''): Equivalent to the [[Ranking Dojo]]. Rampage Events contained three [[Timed Score Reward|timed score]] stages each, with potential for bonus rewards depending on how well each player did by the end of the event. A new Rampage Event was held almost every month, usually featuring either enemy versions of the latest Uber Rare units or collab enemies during certain collabs.
*'''Moon Stone''' (月の石 ''Tsuki no Ishi''): The equivalent of [[Catamin Stages]], guerrilla stages that could be challenged with Moon Stones instead of energy.
**'''[https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/d/%CC%B4%B8%B8%CD%C5%B2%F8%BE%EB Phantasmal Yōkai Castle]''' (夢幻妖怪城 ''Mugen Yōkai-jō''): A special Moon Stone event equivalent to [[Heavenly Tower]], with many rewards and a total of 30 increasingly difficult floors to climb, spread out across 9 layers of the castle considered separate maps (floors by layer: 1-4, 5-7, 8-10, 11-13, 14-16, 17-19, 20-22, 23-26, 27-30). Most floors had rare enemies such as enemy versions of playable characters, Advent Bosses, and even some new ones, including Floor 30's boss and drop unit, [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Miu|Miu]].

==Yōkai Yokochō==
In this game, [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Yōkai Yokochō|Yōkai Yokochō]] (ようかい横丁, "Yōkai Alley") referred to a feature that worked as both a scene builder and sound test. Using this feature, players could build their own scene using unlocked/encountered allied and enemy characters, decorations, frames, backgrounds, weather effects, and any non-collab music track in the game, selectable from a list with the official names of every track. See [https://youtu.be/xiPmEBeZ7jM this video] for footage and [https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/d/%A4%E8%A4%A6%A4%AB%A4%A4%B2%A3%C3%FA here] for more information.

==April Fools' Jokes==
From 2020 to 2022, YuruGeGe had its own news articles created for April Fools' Day, which have been preserved by the Internet Archive. At the bottom of every page was a ranking of fake news articles' popularity that would hint at the next [[True Form]]s to be released.
*[https://web.archive.org/web/20200401081608/https://yurukita-game.com/event/2020_april/index.html 2020]
*[https://web.archive.org/web/20210331232202/https://yurukita-game.com/event/2021_april/index.html 2021]
*[https://web.archive.org/web/20220331160817/https://yurukita-game.com/event/2022_april/index.html 2022]

==Collabs==
YuruGeGe had multiple [[Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarou: Youkai Dotabata Daisensou Collaboration Event|collabs]] with [[Nyanko Daisensou]], introducing [[Kitarou (Special Cat)|Kitarō]], [[Medama-Oyaji (Special Cat)|Medama-Oyaji]] and [[Neko-Musume (Rare Cat)|Neko-Musume]] as both [[Cat Units]] and [[Enemy Units]]. YuruGeGe's side of things featured [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]], [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat]], [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Gross Cat]] and [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Fish Cat]] as both friends and foes as well as Gorgeous and Hercules variants of the aforementioned cats, Macho Leg Cat, [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Mythical Titan Cat]] and [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Hurricat]] exclusively as enemies. Later versions of the collab added [[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|Valkyrie Cat]] and [[Miko Mitama (Uber Rare Cat)|Miko Mitama]] as Uber Rare units, and both were rendered in the Battle Cats art style.

