==Trivia==
*YuruGeGe had the "show and deploy from both rows at once" option 2 years before it was added to [[The Battle Cats]].
**YuruGeGe also had the [[Special Abilities|ability]] filter separated by ability type (trait-targeting and neutral) and the static, more organized [[Catfruit]] Storage layout from [[Version 11.4 Update|Version 11.4]] 3 years before The Battle Cats.
*The Battle Cats' [[Death Surge]] ability is similar to YuruGeGe's Vain Struggle ability, providing area damage after the user's death. Likewise, the Slayer abilities resemble Target Type Killer in that they increase the user's attack power against special enemy types distinct from traits.
*The Gorgeous enemies may have been a reference to Japanese YouTuber [https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%B4%E3%83%BC%E2%98%86%E3%82%B8%E3%83%A3%E3%82%B9 Gor☆Geous], whose signature makeup also includes a black star over one eye.
**Gor☆Geous likely also inspired the names of the collab enemies [https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/d/%a5%cd%a5%b3%a1%f9%a5%b4%a1%bc%a5%b8%a5%e3%a5%b9 Neko☆Geous] and [https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/d/%a5%ad%a5%e2%a1%f9%a5%b8%a5%e3%a5%b9 Kimo☆Geous].
*The Abyss enemies may have been a reference to the ''[[wikipedia:Yatterman|Yatterman]]'' character [https://timebokanturnip.tumblr.com/post/125409360061/yatterman-character-biography-dokurobei Dokurobei], whose red skull masks and logo are often drawn identically to those worn by the Abyss enemies.
*The Serious enemies may have been a reference to [[wikia:funghigardening:Meanie|Meanie]] from ''[[Neo Mushroom Garden Collaboration Event|Neo Mushroom Garden]]'', who is also purple and wears the same exact sunglasses.
*Due to their demonic looks and Forcefields, the Death enemies from this game may have inspired the [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] enemy type in The Battle Cats, which are also demons with a [[Barrier]]-like ability.
*[[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Kagami-Jijii|Kagami-Jijii]]'s attack animation in this game was strikingly similar to [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]]'s.
*While most of the enemies in YuruGeGe weren't exact equivalents of those found in The Battle Cats, there were two that directly mirrored [[Ms. Sign]] and [[Assassin Bear]]. The former was simply [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Kemedama|Kemedama]] holding a wooden sign with Ms. Sign's message written on it, while the latter was an extremely powerful flashing [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Penanggalan|Type 2 Penanggalan]] which served only to punish players who took too long on timed stages. The Penanggalan variant had much shorter range than Assassin Bear but dealt insane amounts of damage with each attack, pushing just as hard if not harder.

